eft shift make infection less likely despite recent cold history", "Stress-Induced Leukocytosis: Unlikely due to normal physical exam and absence of acute stress markers beyond constitutional symptoms", "Cardiac Syndrome: Murmur is isolated and no other cardiac-specific findings (e.g., chest pain, arrhythmias) support this as primary mechanism"], "alarm_features": ["Unintentional weight loss", "Fatigue with systemic constitutional symptoms"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.21551724137931033, "posterior": 0.2579979360165119, "danger": 0.3, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["The lack of fever, left shift, or infection markers increases the likelihood of reactive/non-malignant leukocytosis over infectious or malignant causes."], "evidence_against": ["Weight loss and fatigue are less common in reactive leukocytosis and more suggestive of neoplastic processes."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.3, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.28448275862068967, "posterior": 0.27244582043343657, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Elevated alkaline phosphatase is more characteristic of chronic myeloproliferative disorders than AML, which typically shows decreased alkaline phosphatase."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": [